<LegalPage lang="en" page="privacy" updated="2026-09-30">
  <p>
    alvarotc.com is the personal website of Álvaro Torres Carrasco, a private individual. It has no
    commercial activity. This page explains which personal data the site handles, why, and what you
    can do about it.
  </p>

  <h2>Who is responsible</h2>
  <p>
    The data controller is Álvaro Torres Carrasco. For anything related to your data, write to
    <a href="mailto:hello@alvarotc.com">hello@alvarotc.com</a>.
  </p>

  <h2>The contact form</h2>
  <p>
    The contact form is the only place where the site collects personal data: the email address,
    subject and message you type in.
  </p>
  <ul>
    <li>
      <strong>Where it goes.</strong> The form sends the data to a service I run myself at
      contact.alvarotc.com, hosted by Hetzner in Germany. That service sends it to
      hello@alvarotc.com, which goes through Cloudflare Email Routing and reaches my mailbox, hosted
      by Proton Mail.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Why.</strong> Only to read your message and reply to it.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Legal basis.</strong> Your consent when you send the form, and my legitimate interest
      in answering the messages I receive.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>How long.</strong> I keep your messages in my mailbox like any other email. If you
      want me to delete them, ask and I will.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Sharing.</strong> Your data is not passed on to anyone else.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>What the service stores.</strong> The contact service does not keep your message. It
      only records the date, whether delivery succeeded, and a hash of your IP address, used to
      limit how many messages the same address can send within one hour.
    </li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Analytics</h2>
  <p>
    Visits are counted with Umami, self-hosted on my own server. It sets no cookies, uses no
    personal identifiers and anonymises IP addresses, so it cannot tell who you are or follow you
    across other sites.
  </p>
  <h2>Hosting</h2>
  <p>
    The site is hosted on Vercel. Like any web server, Vercel keeps technical access logs (such as
    the IP address and the requested page) to operate and protect the service.
  </p>

  <h2>Email</h2>
  <p>
    The domain's email uses Cloudflare Email Routing. If you write to hello@alvarotc.com directly,
    the message goes through Cloudflare and reaches my Proton Mail mailbox.
  </p>

  <h2>Cookies</h2>
  <p>
    The site uses no cookies of any kind, neither its own nor third-party ones. That is why there is
    no cookie banner.
  </p>

  <h2>Your rights</h2>
  <p>
    Under the GDPR you can ask to access, rectify or erase your data, object to its processing, or
    receive it in a portable format. Write to{' '}
    <a href="mailto:hello@alvarotc.com">hello@alvarotc.com</a> and I will answer as soon as
    possible. If you think your data has not been handled properly, you can file a complaint with
    the Spanish Data Protection Agency (<a href="https://www.aepd.es">AEPD</a>).
  </p>
</LegalPage>
